      <groundspeak:encoded_hints>3CM BGL 5.4M E WALL REC CENTER

ASC CAP 3 CM BGL, LANDSCAPED.5.4M E OF THE E WALL OF THE RECREATION CENTRE</groundspeak:encoded_hints>
      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="685591607">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-12T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3339080">Gimli*/GeoJoce</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP254 Edmonton (Rundle Heights)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I took a chance today that the rumor was true and decided to try and log a Found It on one more cap.  I was pretty happy that it worked.  :)  I headed for this close to home cap and took way longer to find it than I should have.  :p  lol  Cap was totally cleaned off of leaves even.  And perfectly readable.  Nice!  A muggle was sitting at the nearby shelter over the hill but his back was to GZ, thankfully, so I was able to search in relative comfort.  :) &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Once found I meandered my way back to the car taking pics as I went.  TFTBC OFTH, the one more, and the fun!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684649188">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-06T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="946600">Black Shark</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP254 Edmonton (Rundle Heights)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The rec centre was very busy today due to the lovely weekend weather so Mr Shark let Mrs Shark out to search for the cap while he sought a parking spot.  She thought &quot;rec centre&quot; in the clue meant the building but the GPS led on...straight towards a very crowded picnic shelter.  Oh no.  But wait, it changed its mind a bit and led over a small hill...straight to another packed picnic shelter.  She was real happy not to make anyone uncomfortable (including herself) when the GPS turned her back to the top of the hill where she quickly and happily found the cap just as Mr Shark came along.  Soon we off to wander aimlessly then drop to photograph the ground in another busy area.  You know, enjoy the day in our own way!  TFTBC&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684212706">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-06T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="7458582">mkPerry</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP254 Edmonton (Rundle Heights)

Out again this evening to get a few more BCPs. We drove through a torrential downpour on the way here. The rain held off for our two previous  finds but started up again on the walk to this one. M circled around in the drizzle chasing the GPS signal and kicking the numerous poplar leaf piles unsuccessfully. He went back to the car to check some context photos. They showed he was looking in the wrong spot. Going back it was a quick find. Wasn't going to let a bit of rain and signal confusion hold us back on this last BCP weekend. The cap is in great shape. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks outforthehunt for all the BCPs and the fun I've had over the last couple weeks getting most of the ones in the Edmonton area. &lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
